---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { POLICY_UPDATED, SITE_EMAIL, SITE_NAME } from '../consts';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of use"
  description="How this site's reviews should be read, what we are responsible for, and what we are not."
  path="/terms/"
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Terms' }]} />

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: {POLICY_UPDATED}</p>

    <div class="content-body mt-6">
      <p>
        By reading {SITE_NAME} you agree to these terms. They exist to be clear about what our reviews are — and are not.
      </p>

      <h2>What our reviews are</h2>
      <p>
        We publish research-based analysis of publicly available product information: specification sheets, manufacturer
        documentation, retailer listings, pricing and published owner feedback. Where we have not used a product
        ourselves, the page says so explicitly ("Research-based"). We do not describe hands-on experience we have not had.
      </p>

      <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
      <p>
        Brands cannot pay for a score, a ranking, a placement or a mention. Affiliate commissions do not influence
        conclusions. How we score is published on our <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>, and how we make money
        is described in our <a href="/disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy and prices</h2>
      <p>
        Specifications and prices change without notice. Every page shows the date its price was checked, but the figure
        you see at a retailer is the authoritative one. If you find an error, tell us at
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE_EMAIL}`}>{SITE_EMAIL}</a> and we will correct it.
      </p>

      <h2>Not professional advice</h2>
      <p>
        Our automotive content discusses diagnostic procedures, coding and repair workflows. It is general information,
        not a service manual. Always follow the vehicle manufacturer's published procedures and safety instructions.
        Incorrect coding or programming can damage a vehicle's control modules. You are responsible for the work you
        perform.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided "as is". To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any loss arising from
        reliance on the content, including purchase decisions, repair outcomes or lost profits.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        Text, scoring tables and original charts on this site are ours. Manufacturer product images remain the property
        of their owners and are used for identification with attribution. You may quote short excerpts with a link back;
        do not republish pages in full.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party links</h2>
      <p>
        Outbound links, including affiliate links, lead to sites we do not control. Their terms and privacy practices are
        their own.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update these terms; the date at the top of the page reflects the current version.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE_EMAIL}`}>{SITE_EMAIL}</a> · See also our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
